{
 "method": "Calculations were performed based on principles of radiation physics. Photon attenuation, interaction cross-sections (estimated for 2 MeV and 1.7 MeV in water, primarily from Compton scattering, pair production, and photoelectric effect), and energy transfer mechanisms were considered. Electron spectra and energy loss were approximated. Fluence and dose calculations were normalized to the primary photon fluence (Phi0) at the specified point without the phantom. Numerical integration over assumed spectra and angular distributions was performed conceptually. Values are estimates based on typical behavior of 2 MeV photons in water, accounting for beam geometry and scoring volume dimensions. Stopping power ratio is an estimate for the relevant energy range.",
 "data_sources": "Estimated photon interaction cross-sections for water at 2 MeV and 1.7 MeV (Compton, Photoelectric, Pair Production, Rayleigh scattering), approximated electron energy loss mechanisms (collision and radiative), and typical water-to-air mass collision stopping power ratios. Primary source of data is general knowledge of radiation physics principles and empirical data trends for photon and electron interactions in water.",
